VIEWMODEL.md G19: `check … at f` names a field of the record or case holding the check; another name is E1633 (log-2026-09-28 decision 3), in a record and in a variant's case, a method's name included; on a package-level check, which has no fields, it names the package (log-2026-09-28 U5 calls).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record Level {
  heal: Int
  warn low: heal >= 1 at hael else "heal {heal} is low"

  fn doubled(self) -> Int {
    return heal * 2
  }

  check heal < 100 at doubled else "too much"
}

local variant Reward {
  gold {
    amount: Int
    check amount > 0 at count else "no gold"
  }
}

local let n: Int = 3

check few: n < 10 at n else "too many"
-- findings.txt --
error[E1633]  a/a.canon:5:26
  at hael: Level has no field hael

error[E1633]  a/a.canon:11:23
  at doubled: Level has no field doubled

error[E1633]  a/a.canon:17:25
  at count: Reward.gold has no field count

error[E1633]  a/a.canon:23:22
  at n: a has no field n

4 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
